# Telephone Handling in Spring PetClinic REST (`/home/daniel/sandbox`)

## 1. Files referencing "telephone" / "phone"

Main source:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — JPA entity with the `telephone` field + Bean Validation annotations
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephones.java` — shared normalize helper
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` — create-time normalize + 10-digit check
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone.java` — duplicate detection
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyOwner.java` — update path, sets telephone from request as-is
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java` — create path, maps DTO to Owner
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateTelephoneException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (also `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl.java` — SQL column lists)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct DTO↔entity mapping

DTO / schema:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — `telephone` property in `OwnerFields`/`Owner` schemas. The DTO classes `OwnerFieldsDto` / `OwnerDto` are **generated** by the openapi-generator into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (no hand-written source file; excluded from build checks at pom.xml:301).

YAML (OfficeFloor):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml`

Tests:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`

## 2. Current validation logic (10-digit)

Two layers.

(a) Entity-level Bean Validation — `Owner.java` lines 47-51:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```

(b) Create-flow normalization — `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
    String telephone = request.getTelephone();
    String digits = OwnerTelephones.normalize(telephone);
    if (digits.length() != 10) {
        throw new InvalidTelephoneException(telephone);
    }
    request.setTelephone(digits);
}
```

The normalize rule, `OwnerTelephones.java`:
```java
static String normalize(String telephone) {
    return telephone == null ? "" : telephone.replaceAll("\\D", "");
}
```

`InvalidTelephoneException` (400 via its handler) message:
```java
super("Telephone must contain exactly 10 digits after removing non-digit characters (rejected value: " + telephone + ")");
```

Note: the strip-and-require-10-digits normalization runs **only on POST (create)**. The PUT flow (`owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` → `ValidateOwner → LoadOwner → ApplyOwner`) does NOT run `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` or `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`; `ApplyOwner` sets the telephone straight from the request and relies only on the entity `@Pattern`.

## 3. Duplicate detection

`EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone.java` — runs after normalize in the POST flow, compares the normalized incoming value against every existing owner's normalized telephone via a full `findAll()` scan:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
    String telephone = request.getTelephone();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (telephone.equals(OwnerTelephones.normalize(existing.getTelephone()))) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
        }
    }
}
```
A match throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409 Conflict (`DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`). There is no repository-level "findByTelephone" query; comparison is in-memory over `OwnerRepository.findAll()`.

## 4. OfficeFloor YAML for owners and referenced function classes

`owners.POST.yml` defines the create pipeline (all classes in package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`):
```
validate → normalize → ensureUniqueTelephone → build → save → respond
```
- `validate` → `ValidateOwner`
- `normalize` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`
- `ensureUniqueTelephone` → `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`
- `build` → `BuildOwner`
- `save` → `SaveOwner`
- `respond` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`

`owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` pipeline: `validate (ValidateOwner) → load (LoadOwner) → apply (ApplyOwner) → save (SaveOwner) → respond (RespondWithOwnerUpdated)` — no telephone normalize/dedup steps.

Escalation YAMLs map the exceptions to handlers:
- `...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` → `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`
- `...InvalidTelephoneException.yml` → `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`

Other owner YAMLs: `owners.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml`, `v2/owners.GET.yml`, and the nested `owners/{ownerId}/pets*` files.

## 5. Test files referencing telephone

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`

Important: `AcceptanceTest` describes a **target E.164 change** ("telephone-e164: ... Telephone numbers must now be stored in E.164 form"), which the current 10-digit implementation does NOT satisfy. The assertions:

```java
@Test
void coreNationalToE164() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "0412 345 678");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+61412345678"));
}

@Test
void functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "+64 21 123 456");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+6421123456"));
}

@Test
void errorRejectsUnformattable() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "12");
    createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}
```

Supporting generator in `AcceptanceBase.java` (lines 98-104) — note its comment describing the current-vs-target telephone chain:
```java
/** A unique 10-digit AU mobile ('04XXXXXXXX'). Chosen so the ONE payload stays valid across the
 *  whole telephone rule chain: 10 digits satisfies the early normalize-to-10 rule; dropping the
 *  leading '0' yields 9 national digits, which is exactly what the later E.164 '+61' form and the
 *  per-country length rule (+61 => 9 national digits) require. Distinct from the +1 NANP seed data. */
protected String uniqueTelephone() {
    return String.format("04%08d", seq());
}
```
`ownerNode()` (line 123) sets `telephone` to `uniqueTelephone()`. Tests post to `POST /api/owners` (`createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`) and read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (`getOwner`). `@SpringBootTest` + `@AutoConfigureMockMvc` + `@Transactional` (rolled back per test) + `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN,...)`.

## 6. Build setup, running tests, package structure

- Build tool: **Maven** (single `pom.xml`, Maven wrapper `mvnw` present; no Gradle files). Parent: `spring-boot-starter-parent`; artifact `spring-petclinic-rest`.
- Code generation: openapi-generator-maven-plugin v7.23.0 generates API + DTO classes from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `apiPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.api` and `modelPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (so `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` exist only after a build, under `target/`).
- Testing deps: `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, `mockito-core`, OfficeFloor `woof_test`, `json-path`. Tests run via standard Surefire (inherited from Spring Boot parent).
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (all), or a single class e.g. `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`. Full build `./mvnw verify`.
- Owner package structure:
  - Entity: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model` (`Owner` extends `Person`)
  - Generated DTOs: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (`OwnerDto`, `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerPageDto`)
  - OfficeFloor functions: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`
  - Escalations/handlers: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation`
  - Repositories: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository` (interface `OwnerRepository`) with impls in `.repository.jdbc`, `.repository.jpa`, `.repository.springdatajpa`
  - Mapper: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper` (MapStruct)
  - Tests: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance`

